Tools used in web challs:
      ffuf
      dirb
      gobuster
      curl

GOLDEN RULE: KEEP BURP SUITE OPEN.

Minimal field checklist:
      [ ] robots.txt
      [ ] page source
      [ ] JS files
      [ ] cookies
      [ ] headers
      [ ] hidden endpoints (/flag.txt)
      [ ] login/register/reset
      [ ] parameter tampering
      [ ] IDOR
      [ ] SQLi/NoSQLi
      [ ] XSS/SSTI
      [ ] file upload/LFI
      [ ] admin-only routes
      [ ] debug/error leaks
      [ ] JWT/session flaws

START
 |
 |--[1] Read the challenge carefully
 |      |
 |      |-- Look for:
 |           - given URL
 |           - source code / attachments
 |           - hint text
 |           - flag format
 |
 |--[2] Recon the app
 |      |
 |      |-- Open site normally
 |      |-- Check:
 |           - all pages
 |           - login/register
 |           - search bars
 |           - upload forms
 |           - admin panels
 |           - API endpoints
 |           - robots.txt / sitemap.xml
 |           - .git / backups / hidden dirs
 |           - comments in HTML/JS
 |           - cookies / localStorage
 |           - response headers
 |
 |--[3] Is source code provided?
 |      |
 |      |-- YES --> Review for:
 |      |          - hardcoded creds
 |      |          - routes/endpoints
 |      |          - auth logic flaws
 |      |          - debug mode
 |      |          - dangerous functions
 |      |          - SQL queries
 |      |          - template rendering
 |      |          - file handling
 |      |          - secret keys / JWT secret
 |      |
 |      |-- NO --> Use browser + proxy to infer behavior
 |
 |--[4] Identify input points
 |      |
 |      |-- URL params?
 |      |-- POST body?
 |      |-- JSON body?
 |      |-- Headers?
 |      |-- Cookies?
 |      |-- File upload?
 |      |-- WebSocket?
 |      |-- Path segments?
 |
 |--[5] For each input point, ask:
 |      |
 |      |-- Is input reflected in response?
 |      |      |
 |      |      |-- YES --> Test XSS / SSTI / HTML injection
 |      |      |
 |      |      |-- NO --> Continue
 |      |
 |      |-- Does input affect DB queries?
 |      |      |
 |      |      |-- YES --> Test SQLi / NoSQLi
 |      |
 |      |-- Does input affect file/path access?
 |      |      |
 |      |      |-- YES --> Test LFI / RFI / path traversal
 |      |
 |      |-- Does input get sent to shell/system call?
 |      |      |
 |      |      |-- YES --> Test command injection
 |      |
 |      |-- Does input reach template engine?
 |      |      |
 |      |      |-- YES --> Test SSTI
 |      |
 |      |-- Does input alter object/ID?
 |      |      |
 |      |      |-- YES --> Test IDOR / access control
 |      |
 |      |-- Is input deserialized / parsed specially?
 |      |      |
 |      |      |-- YES --> Test insecure deserialization / parser abuse
 |
 |--[6] Authentication / Session branch
 |      |
 |      |-- Can you register?
 |      |      |
 |      |      |-- YES --> Check role assignment, default privileges
 |      |
 |      |-- Login present?
 |      |      |
 |      |      |-- Test:
 |      |           - SQLi in login
 |      |           - weak password reset
 |      |           - JWT tampering
 |      |           - cookie forgery
 |      |           - session fixation
 |      |           - missing authorization checks
 |      |           - username/email enumeration
 |      |
 |      |-- Admin-only functionality exists?
 |             |
 |             |-- Test direct access / IDOR / hidden params
 |
 |--[7] Client-side branch
 |      |
 |      |-- Read JavaScript files
 |      |-- Search for:
 |           - API endpoints
 |           - hidden routes
 |           - tokens / keys
 |           - obfuscated logic
 |           - flag fragments
 |           - local validation only
 |           - debug functions
 |
 |--[8] API branch
 |      |
 |      |-- Is there /api, GraphQL, JSON endpoints?
 |      |      |
 |      |      |-- YES --> Test:
 |      |           - unauthenticated access
 |      |           - IDOR
 |      |           - mass assignment
 |      |           - GraphQL introspection
 |      |           - hidden methods (PUT/PATCH/DELETE)
 |      |           - content-type confusion
 |
 |--[9] File upload branch
 |      |
 |      |-- Upload allowed?
 |      |      |
 |      |      |-- YES --> Test:
 |      |           - extension bypass
 |      |           - MIME bypass
 |      |           - polyglot files
 |      |           - filename traversal
 |      |           - SVG XSS
 |      |           - server-side processing bugs
 |      |           - upload + include/execute chain
 |
 |--[10] Server behavior branch
 |       |
 |       |-- Different responses for malformed input?
 |       |      |
 |       |      |-- YES --> Probe for:
 |       |           - verbose errors
 |       |           - stack traces
 |       |           - framework fingerprints
 |       |           - type confusion
 |       |
 |       |-- Strange redirects / proxy headers?
 |              |
 |              |-- Test Host header / X-Forwarded-* issues
 |
 |--[11] Common vuln checklist
 |       |
 |       |-- XSS?
 |       |-- SQLi?
 |       |-- NoSQLi?
 |       |-- SSTI?
 |       |-- SSRF?
 |       |-- CSRF?
 |       |-- XXE?
 |       |-- LFI/RFI?
 |       |-- Path traversal?
 |       |-- Command injection?
 |       |-- IDOR?
 |       |-- Auth bypass?
 |       |-- JWT flaws?
 |       |-- File upload abuse?
 |       |-- Open redirect?
 |       |-- Prototype pollution?
 |       |-- Request smuggling? (rare in CTF but possible)
 |
 |--[12] If stuck
 |       |
 |       |-- Compare normal user vs admin behavior
 |       |-- Change one parameter at a time
 |       |-- Fuzz hidden dirs/endpoints
 |       |-- Read all JS again
 |       |-- Trigger errors intentionally
 |       |-- Check cookies/tokens format
 |       |-- Look at challenge title for hints
 |       |-- Search for framework-specific bugs
 |       |-- Chain smaller issues together
 |
 |--[13] Flag retrieval
         |
         |-- Found direct flag in:
         |      - page source
         |      - response
         |      - comments
         |      - JS
         |      - config
         |
         |-- Otherwise exploit vuln to read:
                - /flag
                - flag.txt
                - env/config
                - admin notes
                - database contents
                - internal service response
